gsum char|1)  one third (see also {gsum cha}). 2) The entirety of a set of three. e.g. {dus gsum char}: [all] three times. (see also: Sobisch, Jan-Ulrich. Three-Vow Theories in Tibetan Buddhism: A Comparative Study of Major Traditions from the Twelfth through Nineteenth Centuries. Contributions to Tibetan Studies, v. 1. Ludwig Reichert Verlag, 2002, p. 128: gsum char khas blanks so)
